 4. ✈️ Scoop: Thanksgiving flight boom 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: FAA. (The numbers cover the Monday before Thanksgiving through the Tuesday after. The data includes flights tracked by air traffic control under instrument flight rules.) Chart: Noah Bressner/Axios Thanksgiving week air travel is expected to reach a 16-year high, with 417,775 flights forecast over the nine-day holiday period from Nov. 23 through Dec. 1, Axios' Alex Isenstadt writes from FAA figures. 

 Why it matters: The Thanksgiving rush will test the Trump administration's push to improve reliability and minimize flight delays and cancellations after the historic ground stop earlier this month. 👀 Behind the scenes: A newly assembled "tiger team" tasked with improving the air traffic control system's reliability has been meeting daily for the past week, a White House official told Axios.

