 6. ⚖️ Trump faces wave of ICE lawsuits 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 White House Chief of Staff Stephen Miller walks into the briefing room before President Trump's press conference last week. Photo: Alex Brandon/AP The Trump administration is facing the first of possibly hundreds of lawsuits testing whether it can be held liable for how immigration officers acted during the ICE crackdowns, Axios' Brittany Gibson writes. 

 Why it matters: These cases could force the administration to defend the conduct of officers operating under former Homeland Security Secretary Kristi Noem and now-retired Border Patrol Commander-at-large Greg Bovino. Democracy Forward, an advocacy litigation nonprofit, filed its first Federal Tort Claims Act (FTCA) case on Monday on behalf of Dayanne Figueroa.

 Figueroa, a U.S. citizen, was arrested during Operation Midway Blitz in Chicago in October 2025. Video footage of Figueroa's arrest, after dropping her son off at school, shows officers driving into her vehicle and dragging her out of her car by her legs in a chaotic scene with multiple witnesses. Go deeper : Exclusive interview with Figueroa. 

 
 
