 7. 🏛️ Incoming Dem chairs have lots of Nvidia Qs 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Employees applaud as Jensen Huang returns Monday to Nvidia headquarters in Santa Clara, Calif. Screengrab from social-media video: Zhengzhong Tu via Reuters The incoming chairs of the Senate Foreign Relations, Banking, Finance, Armed Services and Commerce committees said last night that they'll probe these questions about Nvidia's reinstatement of CEO Jensen Huang:

 "Which administration officials engaged Nvidia or its board about Huang's return, and what assurances or commitments did they give?" "What intelligence assessments informed that advocacy [and] which national security agencies were consulted?" "When did the president, the vice president, and other senior officials first learn of Huang's relationship and the associated counterintelligence or national security concerns, and what actions did they take?" Read the statement . 
 
