 8. 🏈 NFL takes over Thanksgiving week 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Sarah Grillo/Axios

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 The NFL is taking over Thanksgiving week, with a first-ever Thanksgiving Eve game tonight that includes a halftime performance and an expanded partnership with Netflix, Axios Media Trends author Sara Fischer writes. 

 It's part of a broader effort by the league to capitalize on holidays, when families are more likely to spend time watching TV together. Netflix's deal gives it the rights to the pre-Turkey Day game through 2029, starting with tonight's Packers-Rams matchup. U2 will perform at halftime.

